    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Drake Baldwin** (68.69) and **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) anchoring the lineup, as both benefit from favorable pairings against mid-tier arms in Singer and Dobnak. **Drake Baldwin** specifically leverages his lead-off spot to maximize plate appearances, enjoying a 10% efficiency boost from the #1 position that pushes his score toward elite territory. **Sam Antonacci** mirrors this effectiveness, capitalizing on a strong platoon advantage that elevates his base projection. While **Miguel Vargas** remains a solid start at 59.34, his value is propped up by a strong 0.380 xwOBA, proving that despite the dynamic platoon constraints, his contact quality justifies the start against Dobnak.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Wade Meckler**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 39.36. Despite a favorable platoon matchup, the combination of a pitcher-friendly park and an opposing SP skill rating that suppressed his raw projection kept him just below our 40.0 floor for preservation of game caps. Meanwhile, the top of our order faces legitimate hurdles; **Jackson Merrill** and **Kyle Tucker** are locked into matchups against elite arms in Glasnow and Pivetta, respectively. While both are trusted starters, their sub-60 scores reflect the high risk of facing top-tier rotation talent. We continue to navigate the absence of **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** due to scheduling, while **Jordan Westburg** remains sidelined on the IL, leaving our middle infield depth to bridge the gap during this critical stretch of the season.",
